Subject: [RFC PATCH v1 0/1] scsi: ufs: qcom: Fix system resume on Milos (SM7635)
To: Manivannan Sadhasivam <mani@kernel.org>,
    James E.J. Bottomley <James.Bottomley@HansenPartnership.com>,
    Martin K. Petersen <mkp@kernel.org>
Cc: linux-arm-msm@vger.kernel.org,
    linux-scsi@vger.kernel.org,
    linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org

On the Fairphone 6 (Milos / SM7635) every system suspend attempt ends
with "hibern8 exit failed 5" and a full UFS host and device reset on
resume. Milos has the same split host/PHY GDSC layout as SM8550/SM8650,
so it needs the same no_phy_retention handling (spm_lvl 5).

Sent as RFC: so far only the sysfs spm_lvl=5 read-back has been checked
on hardware. A supervised suspend/resume run with this patch is still
pending; I will send a non-RFC version with the results.

Development was assisted by an AI coding tool (see the Assisted-by tag).

Paul Schuldesz (1):
  scsi: ufs: qcom: Power down the link during system suspend on Milos

